"Internal Error ()\nciteturn206view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://escholarship.org/content/qt7dg8r8zk/qt7dg8r8zk.pdf?t=rxya8m\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://escholarship.org/content/qt7dg8r8zk/qt7dg8r8zk.pdf?t=rxya8m is not safe to open (non-retryable error)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2605.27532] SCALE-COMM: Shared, Contrastively-Aligned Latent Embeddings for MARL Communication (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27532)\nciteturn206view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27532\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Robotics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 26 May 2026]\nL9: # Title:SCALE-COMM: Shared, Contrastively-Aligned Latent Embeddings for MARL Communication\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Mahmoud Abouelyazid , cite6†Eman Hammad L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled SCALE-COMM: Shared, Contrastively-Aligned Latent Embeddings for MARL Communication, by Mahmoud Abouelyazid and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Emergent communication enables partially observant Autonomous Mobile Robots (AMRs) to coordinate effectively in decentralized multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) settings. However, existing approaches often struggle with unstable communication protocols, ungrounded message semantics, and interference between communication learning and policy optimization, leading to degraded coordination over time.\nL17: We propose SCALE-COMM (Shared, Contrastively-Aligned Latent Embeddings for COMMunication), a self-supervised framework for learning compact, stable, and policy-relevant communication representations. SCALE-COMM decouples communication learning from policy optimization by training low-dimensional latent messages that capture task-relevant planning and traffic information, while enforcing consistency across agents and time.\nL18: Across standard MARL benchmarks and a realistic warehouse coordination task, SCALE-COMM consistently outperforms existing communication frameworks in both representation quality and task performance. The learned communication space yields improved stability, sample efficiency, and throughput under policy fine-tuning, demonstrating the effectiveness of representation-driven communication for scalable multi-agent coordination.\nL19: Comments:  | IEEE IV 2026\nL20: Subjects:  | Robotics (cs.RO)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2605.27532 [cs.RO]\nL22:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2605.27532v1 [cs.RO] for this version)\nL23:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2605.27532†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Mahmoud Abouelyazid [cite12†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Tue, 26 May 2026 18:06:19 UTC (5,898 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled SCALE-COMM: Shared, Contrastively-Aligned Latent Embeddings for MARL Communication, by Mahmoud Abouelyazid and 1 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite7†View PDF L36:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite13†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite14†view license L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.RO\nL43: \nL44: cite15†< prev |   cite16†next > L45: \nL46: cite17†new | cite18†recent | cite19†2026-05 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite20†cs L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite21†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite22†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite23†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...