  * Masahiro Suzuki\nL25: \nL26: Graduate School of Engneering, The University of Tokyo\nL27: \nL28:   * Yutaka Matsuo\nL29: \nL30: Graduate School of Engneering, The University of Tokyo\nL31: #### Corresponding author\nL32: \nL33: cite8†Image: ORCID L34: \nL35: Keywords: cite9†multi-agent learning , cite10†world model , cite11†reinforcement learning , cite12†generative model , cite13†emergent communication , cite14†emergent L36: \nL37: JOURNAL FREE ACCESS\nL38: \nL39: 2024 Volume 39 Issue 2 Pages D-N71_1-14\nL40: \nL41: DOI cite15†https://doi.org/10.1527/tjsai.39-2_D-N71†doi.org L42: \nL43: Details\nL44: \nL45:   * Published: March 01, 2024 Received: July 07, 2023 Released on J-STAGE: March 01, 2024 Accepted: - Advance online publication: - Revised: -\nL46: \nL47: cite16†Download PDF (1513K) L48: Download citation cite17†RIS L49: \nL50: (compatible with EndNote, Reference Manager, ProCite, RefWorks)\nL51: \nL52: cite18†BIB TEX L53: \nL54: (compatible with BibDesk, LaTeX)\nL55: \nL56: Text\nL57: \nL58: cite19†How to download citation L59: \nL60: cite20†Contact us L61: \nL62: Article overview\nL63: \nL64:   * cite21†Abstract L65:   * cite22†References (41) L66:   * cite23†Content from these authors L67: \nL68: Share\nL69: \nL70: Abstract\nL71: Compositionality is one of the most important properties of human language. In the study of emergent communication, methods to induce compositionality in emergent language learned by neural network agents have been actively studied. Humans have individually articulated prior knowledge about the environment, and it is said to be important for compositional human language by communicating based on this prior knowledge.\nL72: We implement this idea as a Reassembly game, a reconstruction task-based Lewis signaling game in which communicating agents have different pre-trained VAE. Experimental results show that the emergent language learned in the Reassembly game showed high compositionality on several metrics than the emergent language learned in the other reconstruction task-based Lewis signaling game settings.\nL73: In addition, compared to other factors inducing compositional emergent language such as the length of message and the number of vocabulary, the emergent language learned in the Reassembly game achieve a high level of both communication success rate and compositionality.\nL74: [Input]\nL75: \nL76: References (41)\nL77: \nL78: Related articles (0)\nL79: \nL80: Figures (0)\nL81: \nL82: cite24†Image Content from these authors\nL83: \nL84: Supplementary material (0)\nL85: \nL86: Result List ()\nL87: \nL88: Cited by (0)\nL89: \nL90: © The Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence 2024\nL91: \nL92: cite25†Previous article cite26†Next article L93: \nL94: Favorites & Alerts\nL95: \nL96:   * Add to favorites\nL97:   * Additional info alert\nL98:   * Citation alert\nL99:   * Authentication alert\nL100: \nL101: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL102: \nL103: cite24†Image L104: \nL105: Related articles\nL106: \nL107: Recently viewed articles\nL108: \nL109: Related journals\nL110: cite27†Journal of the Japanese Society for Artificial Intelligence L111: \nL112: cite28†Proceedings of the Annual Conference of JSAI L113: \nL114: cite29†SIG-SLUD Technical report L115: \nL116: cite30†SIG-KBS Technical report L117: \nL118: cite31†SIG-FPAI Technical report L119: \nL120: cite32†SIG-ALST Technical report L121: \nL122: cite33†Type 2 SIG Technical report L123: \nL124: Share this page\nL125: \nL126: cite34†Top L127: ### Register with J-STAGE for free!\nL128: \nL129: cite35†Register L130: \nL131: Already have an account? Sign in cite36†here "
